## Interface: 16001
## Title: Guidelime |cff66ff66Forever Shaman 1-60|r
## Notes: Braedyn's Alliance levelling route for WoW Forever - Dwarf Shaman and Dwarf/Human Hunter, class and race steps filtered automatically. 1-20: Eastern Kingdoms, Hall of Thanes + Deadmines (24-25 Sep 2026, audited 17 Oct against QuestieDB Forever 1.0.6). 20-30 (18 Oct 2026): Ruins of Lordaeron, Loch Modan, Redridge, Darkshore, Ashenvale + Blackfathom Deeps, Duskwood, the Stockade, Wetlands, Darnassus, Excavation Site, Hillsbrad, Gnomeregan, Razorfen Kraul - every Alliance dungeon quest in the bracket, Call of Water and Call of Air for the shaman. 25 Oct: launch-crowd layer in 1-15, Call of Water finale moved to Westfall, shaman fixes, Dalaran lead-ins carried from 15/23. 27 Oct: cooking + fishing layer (Longjaw Mud Snapper and Mithril Head Trout food plan, Journeyman/Expert steps, fish-to-N stops, Seasoned Wolf Kabobs), drop-rate pass (Never Saddle on Quality retargeted to Elder Snow Leopards; Show of Force, The Quarry's Smith and Slowing the Orc Advance dropped; kill budgets and one-kill notes). 28 Oct: Cooking-175 steps (Hot Spices at Menethil, cook omelets to 175 at Whelgar) so the Mithril Head Trout opens at 29-30; [TAR] tags on the Minor Manifestation of Earth, Kernobee and Willix. 29 Oct: First Aid thread (bandage-to-N stops at 20/50/75/100/125; Heavy Linen 40 and Journeyman at Nissa Firestone, Wool 80 at Michelle Belle, Heavy Wool 115 at Fremal Doohickey, Expert book at Deneb Walker in Stromgarde on the Call of Air leg - recipe values from the Wowhead Forever spell pages). 1 Nov: Alba's Westfall chain reordered to its QuestieDB 1.0.9 prerequisites (The State of the Mines after the well and gill hand-ins, the Moonbrook crates and the Stormwind explosives chain on the Deadmines trip, one run), Harvesting the Harvesters item-start fixed, Blackrock Blockade made a plain step and handed in before Shadow Magic and Tharil'zun, Alther's Mill left to chapter 10, Holy Diver dropped (0 XP, needs all nine beached quests). Gear calls rescored on the 1 Nov tooltips: thirteen quoted stats corrected (Deepgrave Trousers, Ironforge Greathammer, Rockslicer, Flamefist Grips, Bravo's Armbands and others changed in the October builds); Frontier Britches and Smith's Trousers now replace Deepgrave, Staff of Westfall over the Greathammer when no Deadmines 2H drops, Boots of the People's Militia over statless boots, Garb of Florid Feathers over Raptorbane; roll-if-it-drops notes for Blackened Defias Leggings, Bloodied Chestwraps, Witherbite Bracers and the Electrocutioner Lagnut. Wowhead XP refreshed for all 21 zones; six quoted XP figures corrected (Fishin' Time 680, The Powers Below 1,700, Ira's Dagger 2,000, Gleaming Crescent Necklace 1,600, Mor'Ladim 2,750). 1 Nov (evening): Leatherworking after the 31 Oct hotfix - the Totemic Leather Armor / Pants patterns (no Pristine Leather, tradeable dungeon drops) are now an AH check at every city and merchant-camp pass (07, 10, 15, 16) with the early switch in 07; profession notes in 1-6 and chapter 06 updated. 1 Nov (late): Cozy Sleeping Bag chain - ... and that note you found picked up at Alexston Farmstead (05), handed in and Stepping Stones taken at the burnt tower south of Taurajo on the Kraul ride (26), carried to 30-40. 1 Nov (night): Making Do - Expanding Horizons taken at Thundris in Auberdine (11), handed to Baros Alexston with Making Do taken on the Stockade trip (15), handed in at Thundris on the Darnassus trip (20) for the Shipwright's Satchel, a 6-slot reagent bag. 1 Nov (night, 2): Captain Sanders treasure hunt as [O] steps on the Westfall south loop (05: map from the Longshore murlocs, footlocker west of the quarry, barrel east of Alexston Farmstead, jug by the windmill, chest on the north-west coast; Booty Bag 8-slot and Captain Sander's Locker); chapter 07 note trimmed. 1 Nov (rename): addon renamed from Guidelime_ForeverAlliance to Guidelime_ForeverShaman (group "Forever Shaman 1-30") - delete the old folder if you had it. 1 Nov (release check): the Mor'Ladim chain total in 25-26 corrected to 5,340 XP; Darnassus, Razorfen Kraul and Gnomeregan XP refreshed from Wowhead (every route zone is now on 1 Nov data); a quoted-XP check added to the tooling. 2 Nov: QuestieDB 1.0.10 and client build 1.60.1.70753 - the DB now carries NPC ranks: Incinerator Gar'im (16) and Baron Marinous (11, now GROUP 2+) noted as elite, Giant Wetlands Crocolisk spawn count 19 (18); Wowhead XP re-pulled for every route zone (no XP change). 2 Nov (night): 19-20 Deadmines now rebinds the hearth at Sentinel Hill (Redridge had bound it at Lakeshire and 07-10 hearthed to Sentinel Hill); a hearth-bind check added to check_guide. 2 Nov (research pass): Strong Fishing Pole +5 (tooltip); the Totemic Leather Armor / Pants AH searches replaced by a trainer check (no pattern item exists on Wowhead Forever; the Armor recipe looks trainer-taught, unverified). 3 Nov (launch dev notes): Mental Dexterity is 150% of Int, so the central Int weight went 1.05 -> 1.55 and every gear call was rescored - Deerhide vs Duty Bound (11), Town Clerk's Mittens first (17), Carnage Trousers (19), Snake Hoop runner-up (26), two quoted scores (16, 22), and cloth Int pieces are now taken where they score higher (Repurposed Hair Band 02, Kimbra Boots 09, Zodiac Gloves 14, Windfelt Gloves 20, Acidic Walkers 24, Death Speaker and Batwing Mantle 26); launch respawn note in 00b/01b; client build 70755 is identical to 70753; Wowhead XP re-pulled for every route zone (no change). 3 Nov (sheet review): Call of Water total 9,600 XP (08); Spider Leg / Corpse Chopper are fallbacks below Smite's and Rockslicer (08); the Menethil trout stop at 21-22 now says the +5 pole makes it a long shot (09); a Two-Handed Axes step at Buliwyf Stonehand on the first Ironforge pass (02); Eldrun Stormbreaker and Bruegs Kindleborn moved to their DB spawns (47.1,13.8 and 87.9,44.8); Fire Nova is a spell, not a totem (02). 3 Nov (late): Flametongue Totem / Windfury Totem exclusivity note at the level-28 stop (18); buy 2 Ankh for Reincarnation at Ginny Longberry after the level-30 stop (24). 4 Nov (launch audit of 02-26, from play): trainer, vendor, loot and skill-up steps now hold until the action is done ([T], [V], [QC], [CI], [SK]) instead of completing when you walk within 6 yards; every class-trainer stop lists the sheet's must/buy spells with Forever prices (Wowhead Forever trainer data) and the running quest money, with gold checks before the Loch Modan shopping and the level-20 stop, prices on every buy line, silver on the paying optional turn-ins, the level-18 and level-22 tram trips cut (nothing on the sheet), and the Waylaid Supplies ore crates named as a gold source; cave and interior targets get an entrance step first (Silver Stream Mine, the shrine trail, Grawmug's cave, the Deadmines building, Thelgen Rock, the Den Mother's cave, Vul'Gol, the Tranquil Gardens and Raven Hill crypts, Rethban Caverns, the Howling Vale mouth, Dor'danil, the yeti cave, the Gnomeregan elevator - entrance positions from Classic, unverified). Audit and test list: docs/audit-2026-11-04.md. 5 Nov: the chapter 02 gold check says what to do with Mining output - smelt, sell surplus bars and stone on the Ironforge AH, keep Pyrite, 20 Copper Bars and the 10 Copper + 10 Tin for Morhan's bronze. 5 Nov (money check): quest money quotes corrected from the Wowhead quest data - about 40s by the chapter 02 gold check (was 65-85s), about 9g at the level-24/26 stop (15) and about 18g at the level-30 stop (22); Flint and Tinder 1s 32c (02). 5 Nov (from play): Two-Handed Maces is trained, not known at start - the Buliwyf Stonehand stop (02) trains Maces and Axes, the Anvilmar Sledge and Coldridge Hammer lines (01a, 01b) say to stay on a staff until then. 6 Nov (from play, level 13): Mining dropped for Leatherworking at 13 - the first Ironforge trip (02) now trains at Fimble Finespindle (recipes, Totemic Leather Armor check, skill path to 75), buys thread and salt at Bombus Finespindle, trains Journeyman Skinning at Balthus (75 cap), abandons Camping 101: Mining and offers the Kharanos detour for Camping 101: Leatherworking; the Mining lines in 01a and 02-16 are rewritten for Leatherworking (Light Leather crates at the merchant camp, Pristine Leather and Sulfuric Acid bought on the AH at about 4s each per the 6 Nov scan, patterns from Daniel Stitchsong by skill); Pattern: Totemic Leather Armor is a bind-on-pickup Oggleflint (Ragefire Chasm, Horde) drop in QuestieDB 1.0.11, so the Armor is out unless a trainer teaches it. Grind quests made optional with XP labels: In Defense of the King's Lands 263 (02), Gathering Idols (04), Goretusk Liver Pie and The Coast Isn't Clear (05, 07), Redridge Goulash and Selling Fish (06); Banner of the Fallen optional but recommended (Mountaineer's Greataxe). Rhapsody Malt at Yanni for Beer Basted Boar Ribs (02). Record and test list: docs/audit-2026-11-06.md. The merchant-camp crate notes (01b, 02, 06, 10, 16) now follow Forever's Waylaid Crate model: read the label, fill the category crate with one bundle, hand in to Marcy Baker; the crates are tradeable and 4-22s on the AH, so Favor is nearly free. 6 Nov (round 3, Wowhead Forever NPC/quest pages): Fimble prices and list (no Totemic Leather Armor, no Expert rank), Balthus Journeyman Skinning 5s, Camping 101: Leatherworking 270 XP, Marcy Baker pays 5-30 Merchant's Favor per A Sealed Crate and no money, Shipping Label 660 XP + 50 Favor once, Stitchsong patterns 30 Favor verified, Expert Leatherworking trainer unverified. 8 Nov (stat weights from the level-21 character sheet): Forever mana regen is 1.25 x Spirit per 5 s with no Int term, crit per Agi and Int follows the client tables, Earth Shock and Lightning Shield were raised on 3 Nov - Spirit 1.0 -> 2.5 and spell damage 1.5 -> 2.0 in the weights, so: Tiger Band over Snake Hoop (26), Giantstone Medallion over the Golem War Cloak (22), Ring of Forlorn Spirits over Ring of Ruin (17), Whisperwind and Geomancer Headdress rolls and Stormrider's a tie with Defender's (13, 26), Stonemason Trousers first and Smelting Pants a small upgrade in the Deadmines (07), Bloodied Chestwraps, Witherbite Bracers and the Electrocutioner Lagnut rescored (08, 24), near-tie notes on Tranquil Ring and Shilly Mitts (19, 25), the 01a gear rule rewritten (mace racial gone; Spirit ~ Str). Leatherworking trainers from play: Gretta or Fimble in Ironforge, Randal Worth or Simon Tanner in Stormwind - whichever talks to you (02, 04, 07, 08, 14). Record: docs/audit-2026-11-08.md. 11 Nov (30-60 guide, round 1): 18 new chapters 27-41 in a second guide group "Forever Shaman 30-60", levels 31-42 - Hillsbrad/Alterac, City of Dalaran, Arathi, Stranglethorn north, Booty Bay and the Drowned City, Dustwallow, Desolace, Scarlet Monastery, Badlands, Swamp of Sorrows, Riverglades I, the level-40 block (Storm/Heed/Tempest, Razorfen Downs, The Tempest's Weapons with Rage of the Storm, Level 40: Ironforge, Uldaman), Riverglades II and Powderfuse Port; dungeons are required chapters, elite quests outside dungeons are optional GROUP steps, every chapter opens with a level check; Elemental Aid is 3,300 XP (chapters 25, 26); chapter 26 points to the new group. 12 Nov: Scarlet Monastery is split by wing level - chapter 34 runs the Library and the Armory at 36, the Cathedral (mobs 37-42, bosses 42) moves to chapter 39c at 39-40, where In the Name of the Light is handed in and Bonebiter arrives beside Rage of the Storm; gear lines in 35, 38 and 39b no longer assume Bonebiter. 12 Nov (2): new alternate chapter "24-24 Darkshore: the short pass" (11s) for a character already 24 when Redridge ends - only the Darkshore steps later chapters build on (Auberdine and Rut'theran flight paths, the two Blackfathom quests from Darnassus, Expanding Horizons, the Prospector's escort and fossil, the Tower of Althalaxx to Delgren, Kerlonian optional), then 24-25 Ashenvale; pick it from the guide list instead of 23-24 Darkshore. 12 Nov (3): new optional chapter "24-24 The Cozy Sleeping Bag" (11t), played between Darkshore and Ashenvale - the rest of the sleeping bag chain in one trip (the Barrens tower by way of the Talondeep Path and Stonetalon, the camp above Sun Rock Retreat, the Stonewrought Dam with the Hearthstone as the way off the ledge, Thoradin's Wall from the Hillsbrad side), about 10,900 XP, the Old Toolbox and the +3% XP bag; routes and climbing notes are unverified by play. 13 Nov: fixes from the 12 Nov data refresh (QuestieDB 1.0.16, client build 1.60.1.70938) - trainer prices of the repriced shaman spells on nine training lines (Fire Nova, Totemic Recall, Call of the Elements, Call of the Ancestors, Call of the Spirits); chapter 39d takes Learning to Ride and Your First Riding Ram, whose reward is the first ram (unverified in game); the Lost Horse and Karana steps point at their DB spawns; 29 notes in chapters 29, 37, 38, 40 and 41 carry the mob levels and positions the DB now has (Eastsea Raiders are 44-45). 13 Nov (2) (30-60 guide, round 2): 16 new chapters 42-57 in the group "Forever Shaman 30-60", levels 42 to about 48-49 - Riverglades pickups, Krol'dok Stronghold, Stormwind and Aerie Peak, Booty Bay, Tanaris I, Feralas I, The Hinterlands, Nethergarde and the Cape of Stranglethorn, Feralas II, Zul'Farrak, the eastern trip at 45 (Tabetha, the Dalaran crater, Nethergarde, the Searing Gorge, the Explorers' League), Tanaris II and Uldum, Maraudon, Darnassus and Azshara, Un'Goro Crater (in four tiers by required level) and the closing Ironforge stop. The chapters are ordered by the level their quests require; every chapter opens with a level check; quests that start from a rare drop (the OOX robots, Ship Schedules, Williden's Journal) and quests whose giver may not offer them are optional 'if' lines; three dungeons are required chapters, one run each. On required quests alone the round ends at about 48: what Un'Goro still holds closed opens the next round. Chapter 41 now links to chapter 42. Roads, boats, entrances and several offers are unverified by play: docs/40-50-build-2026-11-13.md. 13 Nov 2026 (2026.11.13.3): gear lines after the 12 Nov class tuning (Mental Dexterity gives 100% of Intellect as attack power again, Stormstrike 100% weapon damage on an 8 s cooldown) - the Intellect weight is 1.15, was 1.65; the quoted scores of Intellect items in chapters 19-56 re-quoted and seven take / roll calls the new weights turn round reworded (17, 19, 26, 28, 33, 39b, 54), 62 lines in 24 chapters; Bring the Light (39d) now takes the Amberglow Talisman unless your neck is better; Bonebiter is worn with Windfury and Rage of the Storm banked (39c), the kill-speed model puts the level-40 two-handers within 2%. docs/audit-2026-11-13.md, second part. 13 Nov 2026 (2026.11.13.4): four numbers that moved in the 9-12 Nov data pulls - Bloom of the Heavens 98208 is 1,750 XP (18), The Grand Betrayal 2929 is 3,450 XP (24, both lines), Camp Tent and Heavy Linen Bandage cost 1s 5c at the trainer (02, 03). The Dragonslayer's Lance price (75 silver, 19) was read on its Wowhead Forever page. 13 Nov 2026 (2026.11.13.5): Call of Water is one trip - the new shaman chapter "26-26 Call of Water" (13w) between Blackfathom and Duskwood finishes the chain from part 4 (Stonewatch Falls, Hervdana, Astranaar, Hervdana again, Norric, the Forgotten Shrine, Norric) and ends at Eldrun with the Water Totem in the bag, Mana Spring Totem and the level 24 and 26 rows trained and Knowledge in the Deeps handed in; the chain's steps are gone from 18, 20 and 22 (22 also loses its optional level-30 trainer stop, 24 carries the full list) and the shaman's Ironforge hop in 15 is optional. Golm's ground by Hervdana's cave follows QuestieDB 1.1.1 (x64-69, y66-75.5). docs/audit-2026-11-13.md. 14 Nov: quest order in 18, 19, 21, 22 and 24 follows the prerequisites QuestieDB 1.1.1 names (from player traces): Halloran's chain runs Apprentice's Duties (the north-bay skins, a plain step now, 87% drop) > Crocs of the Sky > Crimson Crate Delivery, handed to Howin in 22; the Fen Creepers come first in 19 so that Rethiel offers Horrors in the Highland and Carnage; Howin's group chain is one sequential block; Vengeful Trail comes before Shared Fury at Forest Song (Kurothel's Knapsack is in the DB); This Land Was Their Land, Word to Ironforge and For Further Study are optional tails of their group chains. docs/audit-2026-11-14.md. 14 Nov (2): the rest of the QuestieDB 1.1.1 prerequisites, chapter 11 and 27-56. Quest givers who release their quests one at a time are followed in that order (Rowland, Benjy Wheeler, Cornelius and Lowley in the Riverglades, Whizzbuzz's pirate war in three trips at Powderfuse Port, Sleebo, Berdun in Azshara, Vahlarriel in Desolace, Arbal in Darkshore). A Fur Trade and Friz's Smuggler chain are plain steps: they open Dunston's chain and Friz's errands. Out, because the quest that opens them is a drop under 30% or an elite: Loremaster Dibbs' Drowned City chain (behind Troll Witchery), Twice Misplaced Trust, From Seed to Sprout, Stepped Out, An Unsettling Discovery, A Small Favor and Tome of Twilight, The Monster Surfaces, Her World, Biting the Hand, Twilight Mementos and its follow-ups, Legashi Horns, The Head of the Serpent and Reclaiming Ravencrest. Chapter 42 is a stop at Farholde Keep; Gatekeeper Rageroar, Graal and the Legashi Cauldron stand at their DB positions. docs/audit-2026-11-14.md.
